   dF/dt = ∫ (∂ₜR + 2⟨∇f, ∇∂ₜf⟩_g + v(∇f,∇f)) dm... and using the Bochner formula and the identity 2⟨∇f,∇∂ₜf⟩ etc. and integrating by parts: dF/dt = 2∫|Ric + Hess f|² dm. The pointwise identity used is the evolution of the integrand R + |∇f|² where the metric evolves: ∂ₜ(R + |∇f|²) = Δ(R+|∇f|²) - 2|Ric + Hess f|² + ... with ∂ₜf = -(R+Δf). After IBP, total derivative terms vanish.

